-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Max Depth Handling:** At the maximum octree depth, the algorithm does not traverse further into children but instead calls `traverse_cap`, implying leaf nodes at max depth represent cap geometry rather than volumetric data [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Transfer Function Changes:** When the transfer function changes, the min/max ranges stored in the accelerator leaves are used as indices into the RGB$\alpha$ map to classify regions [S4, unofficial]. This allows for interactive changes without rebuilding the entire structure, though local majorants must be recomputed by iterating and computing the maximum extinction/α value of the transfer function inside the scalar range [S4, unofficial].
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
+*   **Noise Thresholds:** If the isolevel is lower than the noise threshold, Octree Max/Min is less affected by low-level noise than Integral Octree because it checks if the max value is below the threshold [S2].
+*   **Hole Generation:** Octree Max/Min must loop through all voxels at the edges of an empty branch to avoid generating holes in the rendered surface [S2].
+*   **Max Depth Handling:** At the maximum octree depth, the algorithm does not traverse further into children but instead calls `traverse_cap`, implying leaf nodes at max depth represent cap geometry rather than volumetric data [S6, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision in ray-slab intersection calculations can lead to gaps or overlaps if not handled carefully [G].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
-### [Min-Max Octree Rendering](3709-min-max-octree-rendering.md)
-Min-Max Octree Rendering is an acceleration technique for ray-casting unclassified scalar volumes, designed for scenarios where classification parameters (transfer functions) change frequently. It differs from pre-classified rendering by storing raw voxel data and using a hierarchical min-max structure to prune empty space and skip nodes that do not contain the target isovalue range, avoiding the costly recomputation of classification tables. It builds on [Octree Traversal with Min/Max Pruning](octree-traversal-with-min-max-pruning.md).
